<p><b>&lt;B&gt; ... &lt;/B&gt;</b> - the text between the &lt;B&gt; and
   &lt;/B&gt; is shown in <b>boldface</b>.
    Alternatively, wrap text in two asterisks <b>**...**</b>.

<p><b>&lt;I&gt; ... &lt;/I&gt;</b> - the text between the &lt;I&gt; and
   &lt;/I&gt; is shown in <i>italics</i>.
    Alternatively, wrap text in one asterisk <b>*...*</b> or one underscore <b>_..._</b>

<p><b>&lt;BR&gt;</b> - line break: ends the current line and starts a new
   one, with no extra space between the lines.
    Alternatively, just enter a line break with your keyboard.

<p><b>&lt;P&gt;</b> - paragraph break: shows a blank line between the paragraphs.
    Alternatively, enter two line breaks with your keyboard.

<p><b>&lt;BR/&gt;</b> - paragraph break (this is provided so that you can
   copy text from an <a href="https://babel.ifarchive.org">iFiction</a>
   XML file - the iFiction format uses &lt;BR/&gt; for paragraph breaks)

<p><b>&lt;CODE&gt;</b> - monospace text, representing programming code
    Alternatively, wrap text in backticks <b>`...`</b>.

<p><b>&lt;HR&gt;</b> - a horizontal rule (a line), for section breaks

<p><b>&lt;A GAME="<i>tuid</i>"&gt; ... &lt;/A&gt;</b> - hyperlink the text
between the &lt;A&gt; and &lt;/A&gt; to a game.  <i>tuid</i> is the
<a href="help-tuid">TUID</a> identifying the game.  Rather than writing
this out by hand, you can use our
<a href="gamelink">game hyperlink generator</a>.

<p><b>&lt;A HREF="<i>url</i>"&gt; ... &lt;/A&gt;</b> - hyperlink the
text between the &lt;A&gt; and &lt;/A&gt; to any Web site.  (For
safety reasons, Javascript isn't allowed.  The URL must start with
<tt>http://</tt>, <tt>ftp://</tt>, or <tt>news:</tt>.)
    Alternatively, write a URL by itself (starting with <samp>http://</samp> or <samp>https://</samp>)  <b>**...**</b>
        to link the raw URL. Or, <b>[your-text](your-URL)</b> to display text within brackets which links to a URL within parentheses.

<p><b>&amp;lt;</b> - a less-than sign (&lt;)

<p><b>&amp;gt;</b> - a greater-than sign (&gt;)

<p><b>&amp;amp;</b> - an ampersand (&amp;)

    <p><b>>...</b> (at the beginning of a line) - blockquotes: indents the line following the greater-than sign,
        and any subsequent lines which are separated by only one line break.
        Adding two line breaks will return the text to its normal non-indented display.
    </p>

    <p><b>*...</b> (at the beginning of a line) - bullet point/unordered list: indents the line and adds a bullet point before it.
        Any subsequent lines separated by only one line break will be indented as well.
        Adding two line breaks will return the text to its normal non-indented display.
    </p>

    <p><b>1. ...</b> or any other number (at the beginning of a line) - numbered list/ordered list: indents the line and includes the number before it.
        Any subsequent lines separated by only one line break will be indented as well.
        Adding two line breaks will return the text to its normal non-indented display.
    </p>

    <p>If you would like to use symbols such as asterisks, underscores, backticks, greater-than signs, etc.
